// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27os/fanout.t27 -- actors start actors: a lane splits a task, runs the parts in parallel, gathers the answers.
; Owner, 2026-10-20: "actors must be able to start other actors when a task gets more complex and something has to be
; done in parallel; the answers must be gathered back to the actor/agent that started the task. So we can parallelize
; decomposed GitHub issues and solve them faster. Look how Claude Code visualizes it." Closes #11275. ASCII only (L3),
; English only (LANG-EN). A sibling of kernel.t27 (which stays the tree and the resource formula); this file is the fan.
; --
; DRY: nothing is restated. Links, monitors, exit signals, mailboxes and edits_meet are actors.t27 (used); the lane
; supervisor's restart decision, the global cap, the hold, the mailbox caps and the tree/state/view constants are
; kernel.t27 (used); disjointness of edits, the landing pass (gc_land) and the ready test are golden_chain.t27 (used);
; the 4-heading issue shape is evolve.t27 (used); the traffic light codes are keys.t27 (used); the packer is dash.t27
; (used, read only). New here: the spawn gate, the decomposition rule, the RESULT message, the join rule, the view.
; --
; SPAWN BY MONITOR, NOT BY LINK. A child is started under the lanes supervisor (kernel.t27: transient, restarted until
; MaxR) and MONITORED by the parent. A link would kill the parent when the child crashes (on_exit_signal(X_CRASH,
; non-trapping) = ACT_DIE) and the parent would lose every sibling's work; a monitor sends a DOWN message and nothing
; else happens to the parent (MONITOR_KILLS_WATCHER = false). The parent therefore survives a child crash and receives
; the child's end as a message. A crash the supervisor heals (KD_RESTART) is invisible to the parent; the parent sees
; only the child's FINAL end: a RESULT message, or a DOWN with no RESULT.
; --
; THE FAN, in order: spawn_admit (limits and capacity) -> decompose (disjoint path sets) -> put_* (one sub-issue text
; per child, "Part of #N", never a closing keyword) -> each child sends RESULT to the parent's mailbox -> join_decide
; (all done -> land; failed -> retry, bounded; forbidden or too many failures or timeout -> owner request) ->
; fanin_land (gc_land, children in index order, so the order does not depend on who finished first).

